{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 18,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To the chief Musician, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "A Psalm",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of David, the servant of the LORD, who spoke to the LORD the words of this song in the day ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said, I will love thee, O LORD, my strength.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The LORD ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my rock, and my fortress, and my deliverer; my God, my strength, in whom I will trust; my buckler, and the horn of my salvation, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my high tower.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will call upon the LORD, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "who is worthy",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to be praised: so shall I be saved from my enemies.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The sorrows of death compassed me, and the floods of ungodly men made me afraid.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The sorrows of hell encompassed me: the snares of death seized me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In my distress I called upon the LORD, and cried to my God: he heard my voice out of his temple, and my cry came before him, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " into his ears.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then the earth shook and trembled; the foundations also of the hills moved and were shaken, because he was wroth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There went up a smoke out of his nostrils, and fire out of his mouth devoured: coals were kindled by it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He bowed the heavens also, and came down: and darkness ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " under his feet.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he rode upon a cherub, and flew; yes, he flew upon the wings of the wind.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He made darkness his secret place; his pavilion around him ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " dark waters ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thick clouds of the skies.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "At the brightness ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " before him his thick clouds passed, hail ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "stones",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " and coals of fire.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The LORD also thundered in the heavens, and the Highest gave his voice; hail ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "stones",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " and coals of fire.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yes, he sent out his arrows, and scattered them; and he shot out lightnings, and discomfited them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then the channels of waters were seen, and the foundations of the world were uncovered at thy rebuke, O LORD, at the blast of the breath of thy nostrils.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He sent from above, he took me, he drew me out of many waters.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He delivered me from my strong enemy, and from them who hated me: for they were too strong for me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They attacked me in the day of my calamity: but the LORD was my stay.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He brought me forth also in a large place; he delivered me, because he delighted in me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The LORD rewarded me according to my righteousness; according to the cleanness of my hands hath he recompensed me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For I have kept the ways of the LORD, and have not wickedly departed from my God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For all his judgments ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " before me, and I did not put away his statutes from me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I was also upright before him, and I kept myself from my iniquity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore hath the LORD recompensed me according to my righteousness, according to the cleanness of my hands in his sight.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "With the merciful thou wilt show thyself merciful; with an upright man thou wilt show thyself upright;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "With the pure thou wilt show thyself pure; and with the froward thou wilt contend.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For thou wilt save the afflicted people; but wilt bring down high looks.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For thou wilt light my candle: the LORD my God will enlighten my darkness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For by thee I have run through a troop; and by my God have I leaped over a wall.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " God, his way ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " perfect: the word of the LORD is tried: he ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a buckler to all those that trust in him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For who ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " God save the LORD? or who ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a rock save our God?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " God that girdeth me with strength, and maketh my way perfect.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He maketh my feet like hinds' ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "feet",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and setteth me upon my high places.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.34",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.34",
      "verse": 34,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He teacheth my hands to war, so that a bow of steel is broken by my arms.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.35",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.35",
      "verse": 35,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou hast also given me the shield of thy salvation: and thy right hand hath held me up and thy gentleness hath made me great.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.36",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.36",
      "verse": 36,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou hast enlarged my steps under me, that my feet did not slip.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.37",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.37",
      "verse": 37,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have pursued my enemies, and overtaken them: neither did I turn again till they were consumed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.38",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.38",
      "verse": 38,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have wounded them that they were not able to rise: they have fallen under my feet.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.39",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.39",
      "verse": 39,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For thou hast girded me with strength to battle: thou hast subdued under me those that rose up against me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.40",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.40",
      "verse": 40,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou hast also given me the necks of my enemies; that I might destroy them that hate me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.41",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.41",
      "verse": 41,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They cried, but ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " none to save ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ": ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to the LORD, but he answered them not.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.42",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.42",
      "verse": 42,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then I beat them small as the dust before the wind: I cast them out as the dirt in the streets.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.43",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.43",
      "verse": 43,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou hast delivered me from the strivings of the people; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou hast made me the head of the heathen: a people ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "whom",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I have not known shall serve me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.44",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.44",
      "verse": 44,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As soon as they hear of me, they shall obey me: the strangers shall submit themselves to me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.45",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.45",
      "verse": 45,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The strangers shall fade away, and be afraid from their close places.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.46",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.46",
      "verse": 46,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The LORD liveth; and blessed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my rock; and let the God of my salvation be exalted.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.47",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.47",
      "verse": 47,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " God that avengeth me, and subdueth the people under me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.48",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.48",
      "verse": 48,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He delivereth me from my enemies: yes, thou liftest me up above those that rise up against me: thou hast delivered me from the violent man.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.49",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.49",
      "verse": 49,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore will I give thanks to thee, O LORD, among the heathen, and sing praises to thy name.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.18.50",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.18.50",
      "verse": 50,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He giveth great deliverance to his king; and showeth mercy to his anointed, to David, and to his seed for ever.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
